      "inScheme": "xmet:scheme",
      "definition": "Ring carbon bound to OH or NH₂/NHR dehydrogenates to a quinoid C=O or C=NH/C=NR end under quinone-like endpoint transformations. Phenolic and anilinic children specialize the heteroatom. Distinct from methide-end or shared single-to-double edits used inside methide, iminium, or dealkylative quinoid paths.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Forest QuinoneFormation/single_to_double",
        "phenol or aniline to quinoid",
